{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Native formatting could emit invalid syntax or change a reference containing mixed quote kinds. Empty named identifiers also used an ambiguous quote pair, and controls could become parser separators. All seven bindings now preserve exact Unicode identifiers and values through native formatting, parsing, streaming and binary text output.\n\nThe formatters share readable n-quote encoding with binary-to-text output. Empty strings, C0 controls and DEL use the explicit version 1 UTF-8 literal `~1{hex}`. Every binding exposes matching encode/decode helpers and rejects malformed hex, invalid UTF-8 and unsupported versions. Forced-indentation tests also fixed Python and PHP dropping empty identifiers and detaching their children.\n\nReproduce the original JavaScript failure on 0.23.0:\n\n```js\nconst original = new Link(`He said \"it's ready\"`, [new Link('fixture')]);\nnew Parser().parse(formatLinks([original]));\n```\n\nThe new `ReferenceFidelity` tests in each binding verify exact identifiers and nested values using the same 91 self-authored Unicode fixtures, multiple formatter settings, every two-chunk stream split, binary round trips and 13 malformed literals. `node examples/reference-literals.mjs` provides an executable application example. The expanded seven-language interoperability check compares identical packet bytes and decoded text for 1,392 cases.\n\nCompatibility: this is an explicitly versioned grammar extension released as 0.24.0 in all seven packages. Upgrade readers before sending literals. The prefix `~[0-9]+{` is reserved at reference boundaries; existing names with this prefix must be quoted, which formatters do automatically. Legacy quoted input remains supported, and binary version 1 golden bytes remain unchanged. See the [reference literal contract](https://github.com/link-foundation/links-notation/blob/issue-332-f564abf51726/docs/protocol/reference-literals.md) for syntax, Unicode validation and public APIs.\n\nValidation completed locally:\n\n- Full JavaScript, Python, Rust, C#, Go, Java and PHP test suites; Go includes the race detector.\n- Each binding's formatting and lint checks, JavaScript type checks, Python package build and PHP manifest validation.\n- All seven-language interoperability cases and the executable literal example.\n- Synchronized package versions, generated test comparisons, documentation comparison checks, extraction regression test and website build.\n- Live dependency freshness and all npm/Bun lock checks; dependency-check and PDF Unicode regression tests.\n\nThe prepared branch's dependency run [37849367937](https://github.com/link-foundation/links-notation/actions/runs/37849367937) already failed at its original head: log lines 203–225 identify stale codec/Vite requirements and action pins. A separate commit updates those requirements and lockfiles; the live check now validates all 153 declarations. The first implementation run also identified newer Spotless pins in both Maven projects and a benchmark report still listing 0.23.0; both have been updated and checked locally. Test comparison extraction now includes C# timeout facts and excludes JavaScript `split(...)` calls, with a reproducing test in the documentation workflow. Investigation and reproduction notes are in [experiments/issue-332](https://github.com/link-foundation/links-notation/tree/issue-332-f564abf51726/experiments/issue-332).\n\nCI passes on `d90b6b9`: all 17 active workflows completed successfully, including the seven language suites, binary interoperability, security, benchmarks and dependency freshness.\n\nFixes #332.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-08T21:48:37Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-08T21:48:37Z","messageBody":"Adding .gitkeep for PR creation (default mode).\nThis file will be removed when the task is complete.\n\nIssue: https://github.com/link-foundation/links-notation/issues/332","messageHeadline":"Initial commit with task details","oid":"791f6d9cb6c3cfb3507e317ee45b8775d4f4f9ae"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-08T22:20:34Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-08T22:20:34Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Preserve exact Unicode references across all seven bindings","oid":"dc4dfaa0f5a66ce1a1613d62ff289ceef93e69e0"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-08T22:20:51Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-08T22:20:51Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Refresh dependencies and action pins required by CI","oid":"25de363e6f8bd363086014e45251c968868a18d0"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-08T22:25:50Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-08T22:25:50Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Verify complete reference models and timed test coverage","oid":"5904d83aaa136050357380c2060baf1d58806e5e"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-08T22:26:11Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-08T22:26:11Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Resolve Maven freshness and benchmark version drift","oid":"d90b6b99a176572fd5d9c2be87638a0f49a68f1a"}],"createdAt":"2026-10-08T21:48:47Z","files":[{"path":".github/workflows/benchmarks.yml","additions":19,"deletions":19,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".github/workflows/binary-interop.yml","additions":2,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".github/workflows/csharp.yml","additions":2,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".github/workflows/dependencies.yml","additions":2,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".github/workflows/docs.yml","additions":4,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".github/workflows/js.yml","additions":1,"deletion